   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi!<br><br>I get the the following error a lot:<br><br><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">Warning\r\n (non-fatal rejection): Error in function \r\nstan::prob::uniform_log(N4stan5agrad3varE): Random variable is nan:0, \r\nbut must not be nan!</span><br><br> I don&#39;t completely understand what it means and how to get rid of it. <br><br>The following code gives me this error once for every step of the second chain and makes all lp__ of the second chain == NA.<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rstan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br><br>seed </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">12345</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">set</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>norm_data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>norm_model1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;<br>  data {<br>    int&lt;lower=1&gt; n;<br>    real norm_data[n];<br>  }<br><br>  parameters {<br>    real m;<br>    real&lt;lower=0&gt; sd;<br>  }<br><br>  model {<br>    sd ~ uniform(0, 10);<br>    m ~ uniform(0, 10);<br>    for(i in 1:n) {<br>      norm_data[i] ~ normal(m, sd);<br>    }<br>  }<br>&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model_code </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> norm_model1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data_list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> iter </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chains </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>samples </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> extract</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> permute</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">na</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">samples$lp__</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1001</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## 1000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>While if I change the prior on m from m ~ uniform(0, 10) to m ~ uniform(-10, 10) everything runs fine:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">norm_model2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;<br>  data {<br>    int&lt;lower=1&gt; n;<br>    real norm_data[n];<br>  }<br><br>  parameters {<br>    real m;<br>    real&lt;lower=0&gt; sd;<br>  }<br><br>  model {<br>    sd ~ uniform(0, 10);<br>    m ~ uniform(-10, 10);<br>    for(i in 1:n) {<br>      norm_data[i] ~ normal(m, sd);<br>    }<br>  }<br>&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model_code </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> norm_model2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data_list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> iter </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chains </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## TRANSLATING MODEL &#39;norm_model2&#39; FROM Stan CODE TO C++ CODE NOW.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#800\">## </span><span style=\"color:#800\"></span></code>COMPILING THE C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">++</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> CODE FOR MODEL </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;norm_model2&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NOW</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#800\">## </span><span style=\"color:#800\"></span></code>SAMPLING FOR MODEL </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;norm_model2&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NOW </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CHAIN </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">).</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\"><code><span style=\"color:#800\">## </span><span style=\"color:#800\"></span></code>Iteration</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Adapting</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\"><code><span style=\"color:#800\">## </span><span style=\"color:#800\"></span></code>Iteration</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Adapting</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><span style=\"color:#606\"><br>## etc..</span><br></div></code></div><br>Why\r\n does this fairly small change of the prior get rid of the error? And \r\nwhat caused the error from the start? This error occurs quite frequently\r\n for me so it would be good to know!<br><br>/Rasmus<br><br>(Files to \r\nreplicate this error and a printout of sessionInfo() is attached. The \r\nR-file has the ending .txt because I can upload .R files for some \r\nreason...)<br> <br>"
    ]
