   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Cause of \"Random variable is nan:0, but must not be nan!\"",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "If you want to place uniform priors over m and sd, you should constrain those variables to the range of the uniform priors.  Most likely what is happening is due to a bad initialization, which is centered around m = 0 in this case.<br>\r\n<br>Cheers,<br>Marcus<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Oct 22, 2012 at 8:43 AM, Rasmus Bååth <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rasmus...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
